(A) THE IDENTITY.   Phi_q(s) = (1 - 1/v) log2 + (1/v) F(v s + [1/2 if q = 2 mod 4])
====================================================================================================
  F51 -- THE FLOOR, FIXED AFTER A FIRST PASS FAILED.  Comparing the two sides in the
  LOGARITHMIC form has no usable floor: near a pole, F amplifies the 1e-16 rounding of
  its argument by 1/dist, so a true identity shows discrepancies of 1e-11 and a 1e-12
  fail rule fires on arithmetic, not on mathematics.  The identity is algebraic, so it
  is tested in the PRODUCT form, where nothing is amplified:
        PROD_{j in R_q} |cos(pi(s + j/q))|  =  2^(1-v) |cos(pi(v s + sigma))| ,
  and independently at 60 decimal digits with mpmath (F23).
