(C) TRUNCATION DOES NOT CREATE ONE.   min_s Phi^(M)_q(s) vs (1 - 1/v) log 2,
    M = log(2Q/pi) + 1.  (needed: truncation is a lower operation, so this could fail)
====================================================================================================
  Q =    40  M =  4.2373:  min over q <= Q of [min_s Phi^(M) - point mean] =  -3.331e-16  (at q = 36)
  Q =   200  M =  5.8467:  min over q <= Q of [min_s Phi^(M) - point mean] =  -4.441e-16  (at q = 95)
  Q =  1000  M =  7.4562:  min over q <= Q of [min_s Phi^(M) - point mean] =  -5.551e-16  (at q = 426)
  M >= log v is what makes this work: the truncation loss at the near-singular residue
  is (F - M)/v and the identity's excess is F(v s)/v, larger by exactly log v.

