====================================================================================================
(E) INDEPENDENT GLOBAL CHECK (F23).   Brute-force scan of G over a fine theta net,
    no Dirichlet structure used at all.  Predicted: the only place G dips below
    (1/2)log2 + delta = 0.462098 is a neighbourhood of theta = 1/4.
====================================================================================================
  F26 -- A SECOND SELF-CORRECTION.  A uniform net cannot do this job: the dip at
  theta = 1/4 has width O(1/N), so a net of 1001 points steps straight over it and
  reports a spurious minimum of 0.652.  The scan below is coarse-then-refine, and its
  own validity test is whether it RECOVERS the known minimum at 1/4.
