  F51 AGAIN -- the runner-up sits a few 1e-4 BELOW the asymptotic target, and the whole
  question is whether that is the finite-N discretisation or a real dent.  It is
  decided by the trend, not the level: the identity predicts the shortfall at the
  binding modulus is pure class-imbalance, hence O(qM/N), while a real dent would not
  move with N at all.
