(F) WHY Q = N FAILS, MEASURED.   two independent defects of the r110 parameter choice
====================================================================================================
  (i) the sweep never reaches one period, so the "long sweep" branch is empty:
      N =   8001, q =    3:  max L = N|beta| = 0.333292  (< 1/q = 0.333333)
      N =   8001, q =    4:  max L = N|beta| = 0.249969  (< 1/q = 0.250000)
      N =   8001, q =    8:  max L = N|beta| = 0.124984  (< 1/q = 0.125000)
      N =   8001, q =  100:  max L = N|beta| = 0.009999  (< 1/q = 0.010000)
      N =  32001, q =    3:  max L = N|beta| = 0.333323  (< 1/q = 0.333333)
      N =  32001, q =    4:  max L = N|beta| = 0.249992  (< 1/q = 0.250000)
      N =  32001, q =    8:  max L = N|beta| = 0.124996  (< 1/q = 0.125000)
      N =  32001, q =  100:  max L = N|beta| = 0.010000  (< 1/q = 0.010000)
  (ii) the residue classes are unbalanced, so the mean over m is not the mean over R_q:
            N       q  max class count    min  spread/mean   |G(a/q) - point mean|
         8001       3             1334   1333       0.0008                0.000577
         8001     101               40     39       0.0253                0.003551
         8001    1001                4      3       0.2502                0.009402
         8001    2001                2      1       0.5002                0.015100
         8001    4001                1      0       1.0003                0.023702
  With Q = sqrt(N) both defects are O(M/sqrt N): q <= sqrt N keeps the classes balanced
  and beta <= 1/(q sqrt N) keeps the AP step below 2/sqrt N.

====================================================================================================
SUMMARY
====================================================================================================
  (A) identity                : CONFIRMED
  (B) no dent (min_s = s = 0) : CONFIRMED
  (D) dent on the real G      : below delta/2 everywhere
  => lem:stab is an identity, not an estimate.  The dent fable asked me to measure is
     structurally zero; what is left is discretisation, of size O(M/sqrt N) at Q = sqrt N.
  => delta = (1/6) log 2 = 0.1155245301 survives verbatim, with TWO binding moduli now,
     q = 3 and q = 6 (both v = 3).  q = 4 keeps the equality the theorem wants, and
     q = 2 is the one modulus whose floor is 0 and needs the excess term by itself.
